{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wakeless-laudable-peccary","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# `max_consecutive_repeat` is blind to CYCLES — it scores a real loop LOWER than healthy breadth\n\nThe repetition detector shipped by [rebar:a89d-4dd2-f421-417a] reduces each tool call to a\n`(tool_name, sha256(args)[:8])` signature and summarises the sequence\n(`src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py:213-235`). Its headline loop signal is **`max_consecutive_repeat`** —\nthe longest run of *adjacent identical* signatures.\n\n**Measured against two real traces of the same gate, that metric points the wrong way.**\n\n| trace | what it is | overall distinct ratio | **`max_consecutive_repeat`** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| bf31 pre-fix (264 calls) | a **genuine loop** — a closed 4-call cycle repeated 31-37x | 0.511 | **1** |\n| c827 post-fix (258 calls) | **healthy breadth**, 92% distinct signatures | 0.922 | **5** |\n\nThe pathological run scores **1**; the healthy run scores **5**. The reason is structural: bf31's\nloop was a **cycle over four distinct calls**, so no two *adjacent* signatures are ever equal.\n`max_consecutive_repeat` can only see a call repeated back-to-back — the degenerate 1-cycle. Any\ncycle of length >= 2 is invisible to it.\n\nThis is not academic. a89d's own conclusion — *\"requests=240 tool_calls=475 distinct=451\nmax_consecutive_repeat=1 … It is NOT a runaway loop\"* — was drawn from this metric, and bf31's\ntrace proves a run can be an unambiguous loop and still score 1.\n\n## What DOES separate them: a windowed distinct-ratio\n\nMeasured over the same two traces, lowest distinct-ratio across any trailing window:\n\n| window | bf31 (loop) | c827 (healthy) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 16 calls | **0.250** | 0.750 |\n| 24 calls | **0.167** | 0.833 |\n| 32 calls | **0.125** | 0.875 |\n\nA rule `distinct(last 24) <= 0.50` fires at **call 151 of 264** on the loop and **never** on the\nhealthy run — a ~5x margin, and it would have cut the loop off after ~43% of the wasted run. Unlike\nadjacency, a windowed set-cardinality is also **order-insensitive**, so it is robust to tool calls\nthat complete out of emission order.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis ticket is about the DETECTOR's signal quality only. It does not propose acting on the signal —\nthat is [rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e]'s subject — but c827 cannot wire an actuator to a metric that\nscores a loop below healthy work, so this is a prerequisite for any repetition-triggered remedy.\n\n## Caveat on the evidence\n\nBoth traces log tool calls in **completion** order, so adjacency-sensitive numbers carry some\nuncertainty (the real detector reads emission order from the message list). That uncertainty applies\nto the `max_consecutive_repeat` column and NOT to the distinct-ratio columns, which are\norder-insensitive. The structural argument — a k-cycle with k >= 2 has no adjacent duplicates — holds\nindependently of ordering.\n\nEvidence: `/tmp/bf31-trace-evidence.jsonl` (264 rows), `/tmp/c827-trace.jsonl` (258 rows).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the repetition summary carries a signal that separates a k-cycle (k >= 2) from genuine breadth —\n      e.g. a windowed distinct-ratio alongside the existing counters\n- [ ] a test replays a synthetic k-cycle (k = 4) and asserts the new signal flags it while\n      `max_consecutive_repeat` does not, so the blind spot is pinned rather than re-introduced\n- [ ] a test replays a high-novelty sequence and asserts the new signal does NOT flag it\n- [ ] the existing counters keep their current meaning and field names (the sidecar contract is\n      unchanged); the new signal is additive\n- [ ] the privacy contract is unchanged — arguments stay hashed, never recorded","id":"70bc-ab05-6d4c-45a0","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"max_consecutive_repeat is blind to cycles: it scores a real loop LOWER than healthy breadth"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785943011661659001,"uuid":"085b421b-888f-4b4a-b248-236f68463824"}